<description>&lt;p&gt;City councils in South Sudan are now handling over 600 tonnes of waste daily, most from Thongpiny, while a nurse was shot and wounded in Cueibet in a suspected revenge attack. Riek Machar has said he took steps to prevent further violence in Nasir and Ulang and traced years of bloodshed there, even as disputes over fishing nets were cited as triggers of recent clashes in Nasir. A Kenyan preacher who urged followers to starve to death was sentenced to 200 years in prison, and a UN clash with Sudan over Abyei’s inclusion in December elections has drawn Security Council attention to the region. Coffee gatherings are being used to rebuild trust in communities, and women in Tambura are crossing ethnic divides to promote peace, while a border clinic faces closure risk for 100,000 people. The UCDP recorded 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxNZEhBTlJnSmdvay1MYy00NUpjU29UbnowN0drZEsyYkFPNWY0M3BqQVNQbnJzYURXV2JHY282c1ZETEFmb244azVFeUVIMFlRQ013bzNCSnZWWW5iR01fZWVCNGZRejF4OTBPNks4aktpOEZHVF9MTG5ZempSVDVFTGxOUjN4TGw5eVFuQ1pQS1pkZzRwUHc0Nmd0NmM?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudans Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxOX2lfeDZXX2g5c0FwcUktcGpHR2pyMkNrTzhweDNFcndxN013QU5ZekRrdS14Zm1EWVpxRFZtNk5UdjVTT00xSDg2dUhzV1BOLVVxNXNIcGFhSFJKVDVzUHBtRHNua0J3U091WTh6a2dZb25HNHl3TkF6TDdNZk5MckJYLWFNeEw2N2FCYjA1Zw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Radio Tamazuj&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href